From: boa-z <boa-z@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: avoid folding the module area offset into _end

GCC 14 folds the 2 GiB subtraction and the alignment bias into the
absolute relocation for _end, which places the result outside the
medlow address range. Materialize the address first and apply the
same allocation bounds at runtime.

Signed-off-by: boa-z <boa-z@outlook.com>
---
--- a/arch/riscv/kernel/module.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/kernel/module.c
@@ -432,7 +432,7 @@
 
 #if defined(CONFIG_MMU) && defined(CONFIG_64BIT)
 #define VMALLOC_MODULE_START \
-	 max(PFN_ALIGN((unsigned long)&_end - SZ_2G), VMALLOC_START)
+	 max(PFN_ALIGN((unsigned long)RELOC_HIDE(&_end, 0) - SZ_2G), VMALLOC_START)
 void *module_alloc(unsigned long size)
 {
 	return __vmalloc_node_range(size, 1, VMALLOC_MODULE_START,
